BND-02: look up a TIDAL outfall's curve at the hour of the day

The input reference defines a tidal curve as outfall stage versus hour of
the day, but outfall_setOutletDepth() looked it up at the hours elapsed
since the start of the run (NewRoutingTime), so every run that does not
start at midnight got a tide shifted by its start time. Add the start time
of day before taking the hour. Runs that start at midnight add exactly 0
and are unchanged.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply BND-02_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/node.c b/src/legacy/engine/node.c
index 070db5a..3acf02f 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/node.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/node.c
@@ -1430,7 +1430,11 @@ void outfall_setOutletDepth(int j, double yNorm, double yCrit, double z)
       case TIDAL_OUTFALL:
         k = Outfall[i].tideCurve;
         table_getFirstEntry(&Curve[k], &x, &y);
-        currentDate = NewRoutingTime / MSECperDAY;
+
+        // --- the curve gives stage by hour of the day, so add the time of
+        //     day at which the simulation starts
+        currentDate = NewRoutingTime / MSECperDAY +
+                      ( StartDateTime - floor(StartDateTime) );
         x += ( currentDate - floor(currentDate) ) * 24.0;
         stage = table_lookup(&Curve[k], x) / UCF(LENGTH);
         break;
